## State Class Structure

- Extend FeatureState base class
- Use Equatable for value equality
- Override props for state comparison
- Immutable state objects only
- Generic typing for data states

```dart
// Custom feature state
class UserProfileState extends FeatureState {
  const UserProfileState(this.user, this.isEditing);

  final User user;
  final bool isEditing;

  @override
  List<Object?> get props => [user, isEditing];
}
```

## Predefined State Types

- InitialState for feature startup
- LoadingState with optional message
- SuccessState with typed data
- ErrorState with message and details
- EmptyState for no data scenarios

```dart
// Using predefined states
const LoadingState('Fetching user data');
const SuccessState<User>(userData, 'Profile updated');
const ErrorState('Network error', 'AUTH_001');
const EmptyState('No contacts found');
```

## State Base Implementation

- Abstract FeatureState class
- Equatable mixin for comparison
- Empty props list by default
- Consistent state hierarchy
- Type safety across features

```dart
// @lib/features/shared/models/feature_state.dart
abstract class FeatureState extends Equatable {
  const FeatureState();

  @override
  List<Object?> get props => [];
}
```

## State Transitions

- Clear state flow patterns
- Single state at any time
- Predictable state changes
- Event-driven state updates
- Immutable state transitions

```dart
// State transition example
emit(const LoadingState());
try {
  final data = await repository.fetchData();
  emit(SuccessState(data));
} catch (error) {
  emit(ErrorState(error.toString()));
}
```

## State Management Pattern

- Feature-based state organization
- Controllers handle state logic
- UI reacts to state changes
- Separation of concerns maintained
- Testable state transitions

```dart
// State controller pattern
class UserController extends StateNotifier<FeatureState> {
  UserController() : super(const InitialState());

  Future<void> loadUser() async {
    state = const LoadingState();
    // Implementation
  }
}
```

